WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.738
Simple CASE compares one expression with a list of
exact values It

00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:09.338
is a good fit for direct code-to-label mappings In
this example Paid

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.450
and No Charge map to Closed Open maps to Follow up
Pending

00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:16.900
Review maps to Investigate and anything else reaches
ELSE The row with

00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:21.962
a NULL payment status therefore becomes Status
missing Simple CASE is concise

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:25.588
when the rule is based on exact values It is not the

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.438
best form for ranges such as amount greater than or
equal to

00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:32.700
five thousand searched CASE is clearer for that Run
the query and

00:00:32.725 --> 00:00:34.138
compare the mapped actions
